  "transcription": "$f(x) = \\sqrt[5]{x}\\cdot\\frac{(1-x)(1-x^4)(1-x^6)(1-x^9)(1-x^{11})\\cdots\\cdots}{(1-x^2)(1-x^3)(1-x^7)(1-x^8)(1-x^{12})\\cdots\\cdots}$\n$\\left( = \\frac{\\sqrt[5]{x}}{1+}\\,\\frac{x}{1+}\\,\\frac{x^2}{1+}\\,\\frac{x^3}{1+}\\,\\frac{x^4}{1+}\\cdots\\cdots \\right)$\nI If $P = f(x)$ and $Q = f(-x)$, then\n$PQ(P+Q)^4 + P^2Q^2(P+Q)^2 + 2P^3Q^3 = (P+Q)(1-P^5Q^5)$\nII If $P = f(x)$ and $Q = f(x^2)$, then\n$P^2 - Q + PQ^2(P^2+Q) = 0$\nIII If $P = f(x)$ and $Q = f(x^3)$, then\n$(P^3-Q)(1+PQ^3) + 3P^2Q^2 = 0$\nIV If $P = f(x)$ and $Q = f(x^4)$, then\n$(P^5+Q^5)(PQ-1) + PQ + P^5Q^5 = 5P^2Q^2(PQ-1)^2.$\nV If $P = f(x)$ and $Q = f(x^5)$, then\n$P^5 = Q\\cdot\\frac{1-2Q+4Q^2-3Q^3+Q^4}{1+3Q+4Q^2+2Q^3+Q^4}.$",
